air.<br /> <br /> Now - my understanding is that, no, the defense issue doesn't have to be specifically in reference to 'The Masquerade' as a Tradition. A purely mortal conflict between that CEO and a VP angling for his position - where the CEO cancels the VPs pet project out of spite - would still qualify even though the VP has no inkling of vampires or the supernatural. I interpret the 'Defense' aspect to be fulfilled because the action is reinforcing the human persona of the CEO - aka the Authoritarian. <br /> <br /> I usually don't even use the word defense when explaining to my players. I favor indulge (holdover from Virtue/Vice) or as above - reinforce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}